\image(figures/jump_walk_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(A budget stop occurs inside the mesh without certifying a containing face.)
\alttext(The query lies below the square diagonal, while the only entered face centroid lies above it; the budget ends after the crossing and no result face is shaded.)

The constructor rejects nonfinite points, invalid indices, degenerate or
clockwise faces, more than two incident faces per edge and equal shared-edge
directions. These local checks do not prove global nonoverlap, convex coverage,
absence of holes or the Delaunay property. Those remain mesh preconditions;
boundary exit in an arbitrary holed mesh need not prove that q is outside every
supplied face. Packed legacy adjacency keys also require used point indices to
fit uint32 and triangle ids to fit int.

> Measure samples and actual walking separately

The controlled square grids below have integer sites and two triangles per cell,
with fixed cocircular diagonals. They require no triangulation solve. For each
mesh we run the same relative query (0.37 side,0.61 side) with seeds 1 through
32, and aggregate every complete producing run. The counts include only query
operations, not mesh construction or brute-force validation. The plot uses
explicit base-two logarithms. This finite experiment is not an empirical proof
of an asymptotic distributional bound.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jump_walk_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, samples, tests;
    std::print("| cells per side | triangles | samples per query | mean steps | mean exact tests | min " "tests | max tests |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t side = 2; side <= 32; side *= 2) {
        const auto m = dm::geometry::jump_walk_grid(side);
        const dm::geometry::TriangulationLocator loc(m.points, m.triangles);
        std::size_t total_steps =
            0, total_tests =
            0, min_tests =
            std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max(), max_tests =
            0, sample_count = 0;
        for (std::uint64_t seed = 1; seed <= 32; ++seed) {
            const auto a = loc.analyze({.37 * side, .61 * side}, seed);
            if (a.stop != dm::geometry::LocateStop::Located)
                throw std::runtime_error("profile not located");
            sample_count = a.work.samples;
            total_steps += a.work.steps;
            total_tests += a.work.edge_tests;
            min_tests = std::min(min_tests, a.work.edge_tests);
            max_tests = std::max(max_tests, a.work.edge_tests);
        }
        const double mean_steps =
            total_steps / 32., mean_tests = total_tests / 32.;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {} | {} |\n", side,
                   m.triangles.size(), sample_count, mean_steps, mean_tests,
                   min_tests, max_tests);
        x.push_back(std::log2(m.triangles.size()));
        samples.push_back(std::log2(sample_count));
        tests.push_back(std::log2(mean_tests));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, samples, "samples", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, samples, "",
                                                           {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, tests, "tests", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, tests, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4).title("Sampling and measured exact-test work").x_label("log2(triangles)").y_label("log2(actual count or mean)").y_limits(.5, 7).save_svg("build/jump_walk_work.svg");
}
```
